    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193145_499169_23657" xmi:uuid="23a362c8-bc0f-4f3e-a71e-b068e989bc93" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455117282346_857387_42533" xmi:uuid="42d09eeb-aca2-4da3-8d56-10a8069ccff5" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193145_499169_23657"/>
        <body>A MaterialPropertyAssignment is an association of a material, that is, a MaterialIdentification object, with a material property, that is, a MaterialPropertyValue object. Many properties may be assigned to a single material by the instantiation of many MaterialPropertyAssignment objects.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551193665620_186837_118068" xmi:uuid="ce2954e8-2b90-44cf-bc7f-c6cba8532d61" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847743191_208266_98071"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>MaterialPropertyAssignment</name>
