    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193144_450435_23655" xmi:uuid="ba17dae5-0cba-48b7-931d-65a14eac889b" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455117171001_201848_42530" xmi:uuid="6004175b-2ab0-4584-9f97-9e0776d9c157" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193144_450435_23655"/>
        <body>A MaterialIdentification is an identification of the substance out of that one or more Part objects are or can be made. &lt;example&gt;The entity Part can be used to represent a raw material part, before it is used to manufacture products. The entity MaterialIdentification would provide the name of the material for that Part.&lt;/example&gt; For the specification of the raw material from that a part is made, the object Part is used with the value 'raw material' for its attribute partTypes. That object represents the material item with possibly additional information, like identification of supplier, quantity, size of the raw stock etc. and it can be used in corresponding relationships, such as MakeFromRelationship.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>MaterialIdentification</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193704_798102_27034" xmi:uuid="32a18491-05ab-4728-9ce9-e67d5f6daed6" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
